<%# What the SERVICE would send as a negative prompt when the request gives none,
    per model, read from the mirror rather than written out per row: a model
    entry that carries `default_negative_prompt` gets the print default and says
    so, one that carries nil inserts nothing at all. The two are different claims
    about the same blank box, and only one of them is true for any given model --
    which is why this is a partial over FluxConf::MODELS and not a sentence typed
    into each row (a blanket sentence would be wrong on the five entries that
    insert nothing).

    Locals: key (a FluxConf::MODELS key). %>
<% default = FluxConf.default_negative_prompt_for(key) %>
<% if default.present? %>
  <br>Sends <span class="mono">negative_prompt</span> = a blank is NOT "none": the service attaches its
  print default (<span class="mono"><%= default %></span>) and marks it
  <span class="mono">negative_prompt_source</span>. An empty string sends none.
<% else %>
  <br>Sends no negative prompt of its own — a blank box here really does mean none, because this
  entry carries no <span class="mono">default_negative_prompt</span>.
<% end %>
